Ahead of the second international break of the season, Arteta's men faced 1st-placed Manchester City at home on 8 October, for the fifth time in 2023. Saka was not included in the matchday squad after picking up an injury in France five days prior; it ended his club-record run of 87 consecutive Premier League appearances that was also the longest active run in the competition.<ref name="ARS v MCI PL">{{cite web |url=https://www.premierleague.com/news/3730139 |title=Super sub Martinelli gives Arsenal late win over Man City |date=8 Oct 2023 |website=Premier League |access-date=9 Oct 2023 |archive-date=8 Oct 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231008192606/https://www.premierleague.com/news/3730139 |url-status=live}}</ref> In the 4th minute, Rice made a goal-line block to deny [[Joško Gvardiol]]. In the 28th minute, [[Mateo Kovačić]] chopped Ødegaard down from behind, his studs colliding with the Norwegian's right ankle.<ref name="ARS v MCI PL SkySports">{{cite web |url=https://www.skysports.com/football/arsenal-vs-manchester-city/report/482661 |title=Arsenal 1–0 Man City: Gabriel Martinelli's deflected strike clinches important win over Premier League title rivals |last=Smith |first=Peter |date=8 Oct 2023 |website=Sky Sports |access-date=9 Oct 2023 |archive-date=9 Oct 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231009062429/https://www.skysports.com/football/arsenal-vs-manchester-city/report/482661 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="ARS v MCI PL Telegraph">{{cite web |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2023/10/08/arsenal-vs-man-city-premier-league-live-score-updates/ |title=Arsenal land psychological blow on Manchester City to give Mikel Arteta title belief |last=Burt |first=Jason |date=8 Oct 2023 |website=The Daily Telegraph |access-date=9 Oct 2023 |archive-date=9 Oct 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231009034340/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2023/10/08/arsenal-vs-man-city-premier-league-live-score-updates/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="ARS v MCI PL TheAthletic">{{cite web |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/4941755/2023/10/08/arsenal-manchester-city-premier-league-analysis/ |title=Arsenal 1 Manchester City 0: A title 'moment', Saliba tames Haaland, lucky Kovacic |last1=Lee |first1=Sam |last2=Campbell |first2=Jordan |last3=Harris |first3=Thom |date=8 Oct 2023 |website=The Athletic |access-date=9 Oct 2023 |archive-date=10 Oct 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231010144548/https://theathletic.com/4941755/2023/10/08/arsenal-manchester-city-premier-league-analysis/ |url-status=live}}</ref> Referee [[Michael Oliver (referee)|Michael Oliver]] deemed it worthy of only a yellow and the video assistant referee concurred with Oliver's original on-field decision.<ref name="ARS v MCI PL BBC">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/66974882 |title=Arsenal 1–0 Manchester City: Gabriel Martinelli scores dramatic late winner |last=McNulty |first=Phil |date=8 Oct 2023 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=9 Oct 2023 |archive-date=8 Oct 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231008195301/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/66974882 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="ARS v MCI PL TheGuardian">{{cite web |url=https://www.theguardian.com/football/2023/oct/08/arsenal-manchester-city-premier-league-match-report |title=Gabriel Martinelli snatches statement win for Arsenal over Manchester City |last=Hytner |first=David |date=8 Oct 2023 |work=[[The Guardian]] |access-date=9 Oct 2023 |archive-date=24 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240524195745/https://www.theguardian.com/football/2023/oct/08/arsenal-manchester-city-premier-league-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="ARS v MCI PL TheTimes">{{cite web |url=https://www.thetimes.com/article/arsenal-v-city-martinelli-ends-city-curse-for-arteta-cgkcgh2s7 |title=Arsenal vs Man City: Martinelli and Rice help Arteta crack City code |last=Winter |first=Henry |date=8 Oct 2023 |website=[[The Sunday Times]] |access-date=9 Oct 2023 |archive-date=9 Oct 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231009034210/https://www.thetimes.co.uk/article/arsenal-v-city-martinelli-ends-city-curse-for-arteta-cgkcgh2s7 |url-status=live}}</ref> Within minutes Kovačić then made a similar late tackle from behind on Rice, catching the Englishman on the ankle with his studs.<ref name="ARS v MCI PL SkySports"/><ref name="ARS v MCI PL Telegraph"/><ref name="ARS v MCI PL TheAthletic"/> But Oliver did not further punish the Croatia midfielder, allowing him to stay on.<ref name="ARS v MCI PL BBC"/><ref name="ARS v MCI PL TheGuardian"/><ref name="ARS v MCI PL TheTimes"/> Arteta introduced Martinelli for the second half and sent on Havertz, Partey and Tomiyasu in the 75th minute.<ref name="ARS v MCI PL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Oct-08/arsenal-1-0-manchester-city-match-report |title=Report: Arsenal 1–0 Manchester City |last=James |first=Josh |date=8 Oct 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=9 Oct 2023 |archive-date=10 Oct 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231010040352/https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Oct-08/arsenal-1-0-manchester-city-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref> All four replacements contributed to the Gunners' winning goal in the 86th minute, as Partey's lofted ball found Tomiyasu, who took on a striker's role by nodding it down to Havertz. The German then laid it off to Martinelli, whose first-time shot deflected off City's [[Nathan Aké]], wrong-footing goalkeeper [[Ederson (footballer, born 1993)|Ederson]].<ref name="ARS v MCI PL SkySports"/><ref name="ARS v MCI PL TheTimes"/><ref name="ARS v MCI PL AFC"/> The 1–0 victory meant that it was the first time Arsenal had beaten Manchester City in the Premier League since December 2015, after a run of fifteen league games without a win, losing each of the last twelve in a row.<ref name="ARS v MCI PL"/><ref name="ARS v MCI PL AFC"/> It also meant that Arteta had finally ended his personal run of seven straight league losses against City's Guardiola since he took charge of the Gunners in December 2019, and Arteta had beaten all 24 teams he had faced as a manager in the Premier League up until that point.<ref name="ARS v MCI PL"/><ref name="ARS v MCI PL Telegraph"/> The result moved Arsenal above City in the table and put them level on points with Tottenham at the top.<ref name="ARS v MCI PL BBC"/>

Fourteen Arsenal first-team players (excluding players who were loaned out) joined up with their respective senior national teams for international fixtures in October: Gabriel Jesus and Gabriel Magalhães (Brazil), Elneny (Egypt), Nketiah, Ramsdale and Rice (England), Hein (Estonia), Havertz (Germany), Partey (as Ghana's captain),<ref name="Partey as Ghana's captain 1"/> Tomiyasu (Japan), Ødegaard (as Norway's captain), Kiwior (Poland), Raya (Spain), and Zinchenko (as Ukraine's captain).<ref name="Intl call-ups Oct 2023 AFC"/> Gabriel Magalhães scored his first senior goal for Brazil on 12 October.<ref name="Magalhães first senior intl goal AFC"/> Nketiah made his senior debut for England on 13 October 2023.<ref name="Nketiah senior intl debut AFC"/>

The Gunners returned to action after the international break with a game against 11th-placed [[Chelsea F.C.|Chelsea]] at [[Stamford Bridge (stadium)|Stamford Bridge]] on 21 October. Both teams' performances were influenced by the driving rain and sticky pitch. The hosts went ahead from the penalty spot through Cole Palmer in the 15th minute. Chelsea doubled their lead on 48 minutes as [[Mykhailo Mudryk]]'s mishit cross lobbed goalkeeper Raya. In the 77th minute, Rice pounced on a loose pass from goalkeeper [[Robert Sánchez]] to curl a first-time effort into the unguarded net.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.premierleague.com/news/3744022 |title=Arsenal's late fightback preserves their unbeaten start |date=21 Oct 2023 |website=Premier League |access-date=22 Oct 2023}}</ref><ref name="CHE v ARS PL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/premier-league-chelsea-match-report-declan-rice-leandro-trossard |title=Report: Chelsea 2–2 Arsenal |last=Rogers |first=Jonathon |date=21 Oct 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=22 Oct 2023 |archive-date=22 Oct 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231022100149/https://www.arsenal.com/premier-league-chelsea-match-report-declan-rice-leandro-trossard |url-status=live}}</ref> Coming from 36.6 yards out, this goal was the longest range goal scored by an Arsenal player in the Premier League since [[2006–07 Arsenal F.C. season|2006–07]].<ref>{{cite tweet |author=Premier League |user=premierleague |number=1716016705875390635 |date=22 Oct 2023 |title=Declan Rice's goal v Chelsea came from 36.6 yards out. It's the longest range goal scored by an @Arsenal player in the Premier League on record (since 2006/07)! via @Oracle |access-date=22 Oct 2023}}</ref> Seven minutes later, substitute Trossard tucked in a cross at the back post, making the score 2–2. This was the first time since March 2021 that the Gunners avoided defeat in a Premier League away game in which they had trailed by two or more goals.<ref name="CHE v ARS PL AFC"/>

It was reported that Partey suffered a thigh injury in training on 23 October, two days after the match against Chelsea.<ref name="Partey suffered an injury in Oct AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/jesus-and-partey-miss-sheffield-united-game |title=Jesus and Partey to miss Sheffield United game |last=Rogers |first=Jonathon |date=27 Oct 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=28 Oct 2023 |archive-date=27 Oct 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231027212004/https://www.arsenal.com/news/jesus-and-partey-miss-sheffield-united-game |url-status=live}}</ref> He would be out for months after undergoing a procedure on the injury.<ref name="Partey underwent procedure TheAthletic">{{cite web |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5051040/2023/11/10/thomas-partey-injury-arsenal-burnley/ |title=Arsenal midfielder Thomas Partey out 6-8 weeks after procedure on thigh injury |last=de Roché |first=Art |date=10 Nov 2023 |website=The Athletic |access-date=11 Nov 2023 |archive-date=10 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231110162357/https://theathletic.com/5051040/2023/11/10/thomas-partey-injury-arsenal-burnley/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="SHU v ARS PL AFC"/>

On 24 October, Arsenal made the trip to Spain for the third Champions League group match against La Liga side and Europa League holders [[Sevilla FC|Sevilla]] at [[Ramón Sánchez Pizjuán Stadium]]. The deadlock was broken in the final seconds of first-half stoppage time when Arsenal's three Brazilian Gabriels linked up to produce an impressive goal. Gabriel Magalhães made the clearance to Gabriel Jesus, who brought down a high looping ball, then pulled off a [[Cruyff turn]] to lose two Sevilla midfielders, and played a defence-splitting pass into the path of Martinelli. The latter raced 50 yards, then rounded the goalkeeper to slot into the empty net, marking his Champions League debut. Arteta's side doubled their advantage in the 53rd minute, as Rice intercepted the clearance and drove forward before passing to Gabriel Jesus, who cut inside and curled a shot into the top right corner from a narrow angle, becoming the second player to score in his first three Champions League games for Arsenal, after [[Marouane Chamakh]] in 2010. The hosts pulled one back in the 58 minute. The 2–1 victory moved the Gunners back to the top of Group B at the halfway stage.<ref name="SEV v ARS UCL BBC">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67200844 |title=Sevilla 1–2 Arsenal: Gabriel Jesus scores and gets an assist in win |last=Rose |first=Gary |date=24 Oct 2023 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=25 Oct 2023 |archive-date=25 Oct 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231025004939/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67200844 |url-status=live}}</ref> This was the second time Arsenal had scored at least twice in a Champions League away game against a Spanish side,<ref name="SEV v ARS UCL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Oct-24/sevilla-fc-1-2-arsenal-match-report |title=Report: Sevilla 1–2 Arsenal |last=Rogers |first=Jonathon |date=24 Oct 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=25 Oct 2023 |archive-date=27 Oct 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231027205732/https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Oct-24/sevilla-fc-1-2-arsenal-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref> and it was the first time they had won an away game against a Spanish side in the competition since February 2006 (1–0 v [[Real Madrid CF|Real Madrid]]).<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/preview-sevilla-v-arsenal |title=Preview: Sevilla v Arsenal |last=Rogers |first=Jonathon |date=24 Oct 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=25 Oct 2023 |archive-date=27 Oct 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231027100625/https://www.arsenal.com/news/preview-sevilla-v-arsenal |url-status=live}}</ref>

Four days later, Arteta's side played at home against newly promoted [[Sheffield United F.C.|Sheffield United]].<ref name="ARS v SHU PL BBC">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67179271 |title=Arsenal 5–0 Sheffield United: Eddie Nketiah scores hat-trick as Gunners remain unbeaten |last=Thomas |first=Marissa |date=28 Oct 2023 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=29 Oct 2023 |archive-date=4 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231104031943/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67179271 |url-status=live}}</ref> Saka started as Arsenal's captain for the first time. Nketiah scored three goals before the hour mark, becoming the first Englishman to hit a Premier League hat-trick for Arsenal since [[Theo Walcott]] against [[West Bromwich Albion F.C.|West Bromwich Albion]] in May 2015. Vieira scored a fourth from the penalty spot. Tomiyasu rounded off the scoring in stoppage time by poking home his first goal for the club, becoming the first Asian player to net a Premier League goal for the Gunners. The 5–0 win meant that Arteta's side had kept consecutive home clean sheets in the Premier League for the first time since December 2021. The result extended their longest unbeaten start to a league campaign since 2007–08 to ten games.<ref name="ARS v SHU PL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/report-arsenal-5-0-sheffield-united |title=Report: Arsenal 5–0 Sheffield United |last=James |first=Josh |date=28 Oct 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=29 Oct 2023 |archive-date=29 Oct 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231029061251/https://www.arsenal.com/news/report-arsenal-5-0-sheffield-united |url-status=live}}</ref>

===November===
Arsenal travelled to east London on 1 November to face West Ham United in the EFL Cup fourth round. The hosts took the lead on 16 minutes when White headed into his own net from a corner. West Ham doubled their advantage in the 50th minute through [[Mohammed Kudus]]'s finish. [[Jarrod Bowen]] added a third for the Hammers on the hour mark with his volley beating goalkeeper Ramsdale. Ødegaard pulled a goal back for Arsenal in stoppage time. The 3–1 loss meant that Arteta's side were eliminated from the EFL Cup.<ref name="WHU v ARS EFLCup BBC">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67213052 |title=West Ham 3–1 Arsenal: Mikel Arteta takes blame as below-par Gunners dumped out of Carabao Cup |last=Smith |first=Emma |date=1 Nov 2023 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=2 Nov 2023 |archive-date=1 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231101224539/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67213052 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="WHU v ARS EFLCup AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Nov-01/west-ham-united-arsenal-match-report |title=Report: West Ham United 3–1 Arsenal |last=Wright |first=Stephen |date=1 Nov 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=2 Nov 2023 |archive-date=24 May 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240524195749/https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Nov-01/west-ham-united-3-1-arsenal-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref>

The Gunners hosted Sevilla in their fourth Champions League group game on 8 November. In the 29th minute, Jorginho played a defence-splitting pass through to Saka, who squared for Trossard to tuck home. Saka doubled the lead on 64 minutes with a curled effort, becoming the first Arsenal player to score and assist in consecutive home matches in the Champions League since 2007–08.<ref name="ARS v SEV UCL SkySports">{{cite web |url=https://www.skysports.com/football/arsenal-vs-sevilla/report/498935 |title=Arsenal 2–0 Sevilla: Bukayo Saka shines and Mikel Arteta plays down injury fears as Gunners clinch dominant win |last=Wright |first=Nick |date=8 Nov 2023 |website=Sky Sports |access-date=9 Nov 2023 |archive-date=8 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231108233044/http://www.skysports.com/football/arsenal-vs-sevilla/report/498935 |url-status=live}}</ref> The 2–0 win saw Arteta's side are four points clear at the top of Group B with two games to play.<ref name="ARS v SEV UCL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/champions-league-match-report-trossard-saka-sevilla |title=Report: Arsenal 2–0 Sevilla |last=James |first=Josh |date=8 Nov 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=9 Nov 2023 |archive-date=10 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231110002554/https://www.arsenal.com/champions-league-match-report-trossard-saka-sevilla |url-status=live}}</ref> This was the fourth time the Gunners had won both Champions League group stage matches against a fellow [[Big Five (association football)|big-five]] European league side.<ref name="ARS v SEV UCL SkySports"/>

On 11 November, Arsenal faced newly promoted [[Burnley F.C.|Burnley]] at home in their final fixture before the third international break of the season. Trossard broke the deadlock with a header on the stroke of half-time. This was the 1,000th goal Arsenal's men's first team had scored at Emirates Stadium since its establishment in 2006. Burnley equalised on 54 minutes through a deflected [[Josh Brownhill]] effort. The hosts reclaimed the lead three minutes later when Saliba headed in a corner from close range. Zinchenko added a third in the 74th minute with an acrobatic finish. The Gunners finished the game with ten men after substitute Vieira was given a straight red card for a studs-up challenge on Brownhill.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.premierleague.com/news/3778881 |title=Zinchenko helps Arsenal go level with leaders Man City |date=11 Nov 2023 |website=Premier League |access-date=12 Nov 2023}}</ref><ref name="ARS v BUR PL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/premier-league-match-report-burnley-emirates-stadium |title=Report: Arsenal 3–1 Burnley |last=James |first=Josh |date=11 Nov 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=12 Nov 2023 |archive-date=12 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231112004012/https://www.arsenal.com/premier-league-match-report-burnley-emirates-stadium |url-status=live}}</ref>

Sixteen Arsenal first-team players (excluding players who were loaned out) joined up with their respective senior national teams for international fixtures in November: Trossard (Belgium), Gabriel Jesus, Gabriel Magalhães and Martinelli (Brazil), Elneny (Egypt), Ramsdale, Rice and Saka (England), Hein (Estonia), Saliba (France), Havertz (Germany), Jorginho (Italy), Tomiyasu (Japan), Kiwior (Poland), Raya (Spain), and Zinchenko (Ukraine).<ref name="Intl call-ups Nov 2023 AFC"/> Martinelli scored his first senior goal for Brazil on 16 November.<ref name="Martinelli first senior intl goal AFC"/>

After returning from the final international break of 2023, the Gunners faced 11th-placed Brentford away on 25 November. With on-loan goalkeeper Raya ineligible to face his parent club, Ramsdale was handed his first Premier League start since September. The English goalkeeper put his defence in trouble on 13 minutes as he dallied in the six-yard box and was dispossessed by [[Yoane Wissa]], who passed to [[Bryan Mbeumo]], whose shot was blocked on the line by Rice with Wissa putting the rebound wide. Ramsdale then made another major error on 37 minutes when he tried to throw the ball into midfield, but held on too long and bounced it to the ground just outside his area, and the ball went straight to Brentford.<ref name="BRE v ARS PL SkySports">{{cite web |url=https://www.skysports.com/football/brentford-vs-arsenal/report/482711 |title=Brentford 0–1 Arsenal: Kai Havertz scores late header to send Gunners top of Premier League |last=Richardson |first=David |date=25 Nov 2023 |website=Sky Sports |access-date=26 Nov 2023 |archive-date=25 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231125200127/https://www.skysports.com/football/brentford-vs-arsenal/report/482711 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5085361/2023/11/25/arsenal-brentford-result-analysis/ |title=Brentford 0 Arsenal 1: Havertz the hero, Ramsdale's rocky return, more VAR woe for Arteta |last=Campbell |first=Jordan |date=25 Nov 2023 |website=The Athletic |access-date=26 Nov 2023 |archive-date=25 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231125194918/https://theathletic.com/5085361/2023/11/25/arsenal-brentford-result-analysis/ |url-status=live}}</ref> In the 77th minute, Zinchenko made a goal-line block to deny the Bees striker [[Neal Maupay]].<ref name="BRE v ARS PL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Nov-25/brentford-fc-0-1-arsenal-match-report |title=Report: Brentford 0–1 Arsenal |last=James |first=Josh |date=25 Nov 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=26 Nov 2023 |archive-date=26 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231126121059/https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Nov-25/brentford-fc-0-1-arsenal-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref> It looked like neither team was able to break the deadlock until substitute Havertz headed in Saka's cross at the back post on 89 minutes. The 1–0 victory vaulted Arsenal to the top of the Premier League for the first time this season, a point above Manchester City and two clear of [[Liverpool F.C.|Liverpool]]. The result ensured the Gunners extended their run to 17 games unbeaten in [[London derbies]] in the Premier League (W12 D5).<ref name="BRE v ARS PL SkySports"/> Arteta became the 10th manager in Arsenal history to reach 200 games in charge. He had won 116 games, the most wins of any manager in their first 200 games in charge of the Gunners (previously Arsène Wenger with 111).<ref name="BRE v ARS PL SkySports"/>

