On 28 November, Arteta confirmed in the pre-match press conference that Vieira had undergone surgery to his groin and would be out for weeks.<ref name="Vieira underwent surgery BBC">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67561012 |title=Fabio Vieira: Arsenal midfielder 'out for weeks' with groin injury |date=28 Nov 2023 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=29 Nov 2023 |archive-date=29 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231129023258/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67561012 |url-status=live}}</ref> A day later, Arsenal played at home in their fifth Champions League group game against Lens, who had beaten them 2–1 in the reverse fixture in October. The match saw several records set. Havertz tucked home from close range on 13 minutes,<ref name="ARS v LEN UCL BBC">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67558709 |title=Arsenal 6–0 Lens: Gunners win Champions League group with first-half rout |last=Smith |first=Emma |date=29 Nov 2023 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=30 Nov 2023 |archive-date=30 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231130002307/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67558709 |url-status=live}}</ref> becoming the 100th different Arsenal player to score a goal for the Gunners at Emirates Stadium since the club moved from [[Arsenal Stadium|Highbury]] in 2006.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/can-you-name-our-101-goalscorers-emirates |title=Can you name our 101 goalscorers at the Emirates? |date=30 Nov 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=30 Nov 2023 |archive-date=2 Dec 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231202043227/https://www.arsenal.com/news/can-you-name-our-101-goalscorers-emirates |url-status=live}}</ref> In the 21st minute, Gabriel Jesus collected a Saka pass and slotted the ball past visiting goalkeeper,<ref name="ARS v LEN UCL BBC"/> becoming the first player to score in each of his first four Champions League appearances for an English side. This also made Saka the first Premier League player to reach ten assists in all competitions this season.<ref name="ARS v LEN UCL SkySports">{{cite web |url=https://www.skysports.com/football/arsenal-vs-rc-lens/report/498951 |title=Arsenal 6–0 RC Lens: Gunners through to Champions League last-16 as Group B winners after stunning first half |last=Marsh |first=Charlotte |date=29 Nov 2023 |website=Sky Sports |access-date=30 Nov 2023 |archive-date=29 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231129233127/http://www.skysports.com/football/arsenal-vs-rc-lens/report/498951 |url-status=live}}</ref> Saka added a third on 23 minutes,<ref name="ARS v LEN UCL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Nov-29/arsenal-rc-lens-match-report |title=Report: Arsenal 6–0 RC Lens |last=Wright |first=Stephen |date=29 Nov 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=30 Nov 2023 |archive-date=2 Dec 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231202054831/https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Nov-29/arsenal-rc-lens-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref> becoming the first player to both score and assist in three consecutive home games in the Champions League since 2015–16.<ref name="ARS v LEN UCL SkySports"/> Four minutes later, Tomiyasu's ball from the right-back position found Martinelli, who raced away down the left flank, then cut inside and curled a shot into the far corner. This was the fastest an English club had scored four goals in a Champions League match since 1998.<ref name="ARS v LEN UCL SkySports"/> In first-half stoppage time, Tomiyasu crossed for Ødegaard to thump a volley into the back of the net.<ref name="ARS v LEN UCL AFC"/> Arsenal became the first team in Champions League history to have five different scorers (excluding own goals) in the first half of a game.<ref name="ARS v LEN UCL SkySports"/> In the 86th minute, substitute Jorginho converted his first Arsenal goal from the penalty spot.<ref name="ARS v LEN UCL TheAthletic">{{cite web |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5093399/2023/11/29/arsenal-lens-result-analysis/ |title=Arsenal 6–0 Lens: Jesus can finish, a front five to fear and qualification secured |last=Campbell |first=Jordan |date=29 Nov 2023 |website=The Athletic |access-date=30 Nov 2023 |archive-date=30 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231130044729/https://theathletic.com/5093399/2023/11/29/arsenal-lens-result-analysis/ |url-status=live}}</ref> The emphatic 6–0 victory was the biggest ever win by an English side against a French opponent in European competition.<ref name="ARS v LEN UCL SkySports"/> The result ensured Arteta's side qualified for the [[2023–24 UEFA Champions League knockout phase|Champions League knockout stage]] as Group B winners with a game to spare.<ref name="ARS v LEN UCL BBC"/>

====Newcastle match, Arteta comments, FA charge and hearing====
Arsenal headed to the north east of England on 4 November facing 6th-placed [[Newcastle United F.C.|Newcastle United]] at [[St James' Park]]. White made his 100th appearance for the Gunners, while Ødegaard was unfit and missed out on a matchday squad for the first time since September 2022.<ref name="NEW v ARS PL line-up AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/team-news-havertz-starts-odegaard-misses-out |title=Team news: Havertz starts, Odegaard misses out |last=Rogers |first=Jonathon |date=4 Nov 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=5 Nov 2023 |archive-date=4 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231104204559/https://www.arsenal.com/news/team-news-havertz-starts-odegaard-misses-out |url-status=live}}</ref>

In the 30th minute, Saka was hacked down from behind by the Magpies' defender [[Dan Burn]]. Just a minute later, Saka was chopped down from behind by the same player again.<ref name="NEW v ARS PL BBC 3 p6">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/67065667/page/6 |title=Premier League: Newcastle end Arsenal's unbeaten start to season – reaction (page 6) |last=Rose |first=Gary |date=4 Nov 2023 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=5 Nov 2023 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231217021254/https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/67065667/page/6 |archive-date=17 Dec 2023}}</ref><ref name="NEW v ARS PL Telegraph">{{cite web |url=https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2023/11/04/newcastle-vs-arsenal-premier-league-live-score-updates/ |title=Anthony Gordon winner survives hat-trick of Var checks to infuriate Arsenal |last=Edwards |first=Luke |date=4 Nov 2023 |website=The Daily Telegraph |access-date=5 Nov 2023 |url-status=live |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231217080019/https://www.telegraph.co.uk/football/2023/11/04/newcastle-vs-arsenal-premier-league-live-score-updates/ |archive-date=17 Dec 2023}}</ref><ref name="NEW v ARS PL TheAthletic 2">{{cite web |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5030819/2023/11/05/arsenal-creativity-saka-newcastle/ |title=Arsenal struggle to create again – Saka being glued to the touchline does not help |last=Campbell |first=Jordan |date=5 Nov 2023 |website=The Athletic |access-date=5 Nov 2023 |archive-date=6 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231106041818/https://theathletic.com/5030819/2023/11/05/arsenal-creativity-saka-newcastle/ |url-status=live}}</ref> Several Arsenal players complained to the referee [[Stuart Attwell]], but Burn escaped without a yellow card.<ref name="NEW v ARS PL BBC 3 p6"/><ref name="NEW v ARS PL Telegraph"/><ref name="NEW v ARS PL TheAthletic 2"/>

In the 37th minute, Havertz challenged [[Sean Longstaff]] earning him a yellow card. The VAR check was quick and the referee's original decision stood.<ref name="NEW v ARS PL Telegraph"/><ref name="NEW v ARS PL BBC 3 p5">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/67065667/page/5 |title=Premier League: Newcastle end Arsenal's unbeaten start to season – reaction (page 5) |last=Rose |first=Gary |date=4 Nov 2023 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=5 Nov 2023 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231217021411/https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/67065667/page/5 |archive-date=17 Dec 2023}}</ref> Upon replay, the Germany international missed Longstaff completely with his leading leg and only caught him with his trailing leg that was fully bent in the follow-through.<ref name="NEW v ARS PL Telegraph"/><ref name="NEW v ARS PL BBC 3 p5"/><ref name="NEW v ARS PL Talksport 1">{{cite web |url=https://talksport.com/football/1629300/kai-havertz-escapes-red-graeme-souness-newcastle-arsenal/ |title=Kai Havertz escapes red card for 'Graeme Souness tackle' but THREE Newcastle players booked |last=Calcutt |first=Robert |date=4 Nov 2023 |website=[[Talksport]] |access-date=5 Nov 2023 |archive-date=4 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231104191206/https://talksport.com/football/1629300/kai-havertz-escapes-red-graeme-souness-newcastle-arsenal/ |url-status=live}}</ref> The challenge sparked a players' melee that took referee Attwell some time to control, with three Newcastle players including Longstaff shown yellow cards.<ref name="NEW v ARS PL Telegraph"/><ref name="NEW v ARS PL Talksport 1"/><ref name="NEW v ARS PL SkySports">{{cite web |url=https://www.skysports.com/football/newcastle-united-vs-arsenal/report/482697 |title=Newcastle 1–0 Arsenal: Anthony Gordon's second-half strike ends Gunners' unbeaten start to Premier League season |date=4 Nov 2023 |website=Sky Sports |access-date=5 Nov 2023 |archive-date=4 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231104223035/https://www.skysports.com/football/newcastle-united-vs-arsenal/report/482697 |url-status=live}}</ref>

Having missed a slide tackle on White in the 45th minute, Newcastle midfielder [[Bruno Guimarães]] challenged Jorginho from behind and elbowed the latter in the back of the head after the ball had gone, leaving the Italian crocked on the ground.<ref name="NEW v ARS PL Talksport 2">{{cite web |url=https://talksport.com/football/1629303/bruno-guimaraes-jorginho-red-card-arsenal-newcastle/ |title=Newcastle star Bruno Guimaraes avoids sending off for elbowing Jorginho before confronting Declan Rice |last=Vurley |first=Callum |date=4 Nov 2023 |website=Talksport |access-date=5 Nov 2023 |archive-date=13 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231113004702/https://talksport.com/football/1629303/bruno-guimaraes-jorginho-red-card-arsenal-newcastle/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="NEW v ARS PL NBC10Philadelphia">{{cite web |url=https://www.nbcphiladelphia.com/news/sports/soccer/absolute-disgrace-arsenal-manager-slams-epl-officiating-after-triple-var-check-vs-newcastle/3686949/ |title='Absolute disgrace': Arsenal manager slams EPL officiating after triple VAR check vs. Newcastle |last=Singh |first=Sanjesh |date=4 Nov 2023 |website=[[NBC10 Philadelphia]] |access-date=5 Nov 2023 |archive-date=4 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231104215027/https://www.nbcphiladelphia.com/news/sports/soccer/absolute-disgrace-arsenal-manager-slams-epl-officiating-after-triple-var-check-vs-newcastle/3686949/ |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="NEW v ARS PL BBC">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67247519 |title=Newcastle United 1–0 Arsenal: Anthony Gordon hands Gunners first Premier League defeat of season |last=McNulty |first=Phil |date=4 Nov 2023 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=5 Nov 2023 |archive-date=5 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231105004537/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67247519 |url-status=live}}</ref> The VAR did have a look, but did not deem it worthy of a yellow or red card.<ref name="NEW v ARS PL Talksport 2"/><ref name="NEW v ARS PL NBC10Philadelphia"/><ref name="NEW v ARS PL BBC"/> Guimarães escaped punishment again near the hour mark as he barged into the back of Jorginho off the ball, and then raised his hand to urge the Italian to get up.<ref name="NEW v ARS PL FoxSportsAustralia">{{cite web |url=https://www.foxsports.com.au/football/premier-league/epl-2023-scores-results-updates-latest-newcastle-defeat-arsenal-var-goal-controversy-mikel-arteta-comments-video-manchester-city-defeat-bournemouth-erling-haaland-injury/news-story/74b5d6a34fbf9aaf50d2d5778b483121 |title='Feel sick': Gunners stunned in 'disgraceful' controversy; superstar's scare mars mauling: PL Wrap |date=4 Nov 2023 |website=[[Fox Sports (Australia)|Fox Sports Australia]] |access-date=5 Nov 2023 |archive-date=5 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231105015958/https://www.foxsports.com.au/football/premier-league/epl-2023-scores-results-updates-latest-newcastle-defeat-arsenal-var-goal-controversy-mikel-arteta-comments-video-manchester-city-defeat-bournemouth-erling-haaland-injury/news-story/74b5d6a34fbf9aaf50d2d5778b483121 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="NEW v ARS PL Telegraph"/><ref name="NEW v ARS PL BBC 3 p3">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/67065667/page/3 |title=Premier League: Newcastle end Arsenal's unbeaten start to season – reaction (page 3) |last=Rose |first=Gary |date=4 Nov 2023 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=5 Nov 2023 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231217022148/https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/67065667/page/3 |archive-date=17 Dec 2023}}</ref>

In the 63rd minute, Newcastle midfielder [[Joe Willock]] chased down a mishit shot by [[Jacob Murphy]] that appeared to be going out for an Arsenal goal-kick. But he managed to retrieve the ball by the corner flag, subsequently lofting a cross into the back post to [[Joelinton]], who two-handed pushed defender Gabriel Magalhães in the back and headed the ball to an unmarked [[Anthony Gordon (footballer)|Anthony Gordon]] for a close-range finish.<ref name="NEW v ARS PL SkySports"/><ref name="Arteta cleared of FA charge football.london">{{cite web |url=https://www.football.london/arsenal-fc/news/breaking-arsenal-boss-mikel-arteta-28282398 |title=Arsenal boss Mikel Arteta cleared of FA misconduct charge after Newcastle VAR rant |last=Kaynak |first=Kaya |date=14 Dec 2023 |website=football.london |access-date=14 Dec 2023 |archive-date=14 Dec 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231214163047/https://www.football.london/arsenal-fc/news/breaking-arsenal-boss-mikel-arteta-28282398 |url-status=live}}</ref> The VAR took four minutes and six seconds to check three different possible infringements:<ref name="NEW v ARS PL SkySports"/><ref name="NEW v ARS PL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Nov-04/newcastle-united-1-0-arsenal-match-report |title=Report: Newcastle United 1–0 Arsenal |last=Rogers |first=Jonathon |date=4 Nov 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=5 Nov 2023 |archive-date=4 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231104204558/https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Nov-04/newcastle-united-1-0-arsenal-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref> whether the ball was out of play before Willock crossed it into the box, whether Joelinton committed a foul on Gabriel Magalhães when he received the cross, and whether Gordon was offside when the ball was bundled into his path.<ref name="Arteta cleared of FA charge football.london"/><ref name="Arteta cleared of FA charge TheAthletic">{{cite web |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5138309/2023/12/15/explaining-mikel-arteta-not-guilty-written-reasons/ |title=Why was Mikel Arteta not guilty? Explaining the FA's written reasons |last=Whitehead |first=Jacob |date=15 Dec 2023 |website=The Athletic |access-date=15 Dec 2023 |archive-date=15 Dec 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231215070142/https://theathletic.com/5138309/2023/12/15/explaining-mikel-arteta-not-guilty-written-reasons/ |url-status=live}}</ref> However, all three were controversially cleared and the goal was eventually allowed.<ref name="NEW v ARS PL NBC10Philadelphia"/><ref name="NEW v ARS PL FoxSportsAustralia"/><ref name="Arteta cleared of FA charge football.london"/>

In the 88th minute, Guimarães shoved substitute Vieira off the ball with a push to the face of the Arsenal player, and was finally shown the yellow card.<ref name="NEW v ARS PL Telegraph"/><ref name="NEW v ARS PL BBC 3 p2">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/67065667/page/2 |title=Premier League: Newcastle end Arsenal's unbeaten start to season – reaction (page 2) |last=Rose |first=Gary |date=4 Nov 2023 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=5 Nov 2023 |url-status=dead |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231217022251/https://www.bbc.com/sport/live/football/67065667/page/2 |archive-date=17 Dec 2023}}</ref> Two minutes later, Newcastle defender [[Valentino Livramento]] made a late tackle from behind on Martinelli, taking the Arsenal winger down on the touchline and receiving a yellow card.<ref name="NEW v ARS PL Telegraph"/><ref name="NEW v ARS PL BBC 3 p2"/> The match ended 1–0 for the hosts. It was the first time the Gunners lost in the Premier League this season.<ref name="NEW v ARS PL AFC"/>

In his post-match interview, Arsenal manager Arteta said: "We didn't deserve to lose the match. We lost the match because of the clear and obvious decisions. It's embarrassing. A disgrace."<ref name="NEW v ARS PL SkySports"/><ref name="NEW v ARS PL BBC 2">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67323707 |title=Newcastle United 1–0 Arsenal: Mikel Arteta calls VAR decision to award goal 'a disgrace' |last=Begley |first=Emlyn |date=4 Nov 2023 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=5 Nov 2023 |archive-date=4 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231104233814/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67323707 |url-status=live}}</ref> He continued: "It's embarrassing what happened – how this goal stands, in the Premier League – this league we say is the best in the world. I've been 20 years in this country and now I feel ashamed. It's a disgrace and there's too much at stake here."<ref name="NEW v ARS PL BBC 2"/><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/every-word-mikels-post-newcastle-presser-0 |title=Every word from Mikel's post-Newcastle presser |date=4 Nov 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=5 Nov 2023 |archive-date=5 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231105122325/https://www.arsenal.com/news/every-word-mikels-post-newcastle-presser-0 |url-status=live}}</ref> The following morning, Arsenal's official website released a club statement claiming that the club "wholeheartedly supports" Arteta's comments following the match, furthering "The Premier League is the best league in the world with the best players, coaches and supporters, all of whom deserve better. [[PGMOL]] urgently needs to address the standard of officiating and focus on action which moves us all on from retrospective analysis, attempted explanations and apologies".<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/club-statement-1 |title=Club statement |date=5 Nov 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=5 Nov 2023 |archive-date=5 Nov 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231105142158/https://www.arsenal.com/news/club-statement-1 |url-status=live}}</ref>

On 16 November, [[the Football Association]], England's national governing body, charged Arteta with a breach of Rule E3.1 – that his words after the game against Newcastle were "insulting towards match officials and/or detrimental to the game and/or bring the game into disrepute".<ref name="Arteta cleared of FA charge TheAthletic"/>

On 7 December, a hearing was held at Wembley Stadium in front of the FA's independent Regulatory Commission. Arteta's legal team was led by Ian Mill [[King's Counsel|KC]], a member of [[Blackstone Chambers]].<ref name="The FA v Mikel Arteta FA PDF">{{cite web |url=https://www.thefa.com/-/media/thefacom-new/files/rules-and-regulations/2023-24/the-fa-v-mikel-arteta---written-reasons.ashx |title=The FA v Mikel Arteta – Written Reasons |date=7 Dec 2023 |website=The Football Association |format=PDF |access-date=14 Dec 2023 |archive-date=17 Dec 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231217005538/http://www.thefa.com/-/media/thefacom-new/files/rules-and-regulations/2023-24/the-fa-v-mikel-arteta---written-reasons.ashx |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="Arteta cleared of FA charge TheAthletic"/>

A week later, the FA said in a statement that the independent Regulatory Commission found the charge against Arteta to be not proven.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.thefa.com/news/2023/dec/14/update-on-mikel-arteta-charge |title=Update on alleged FA Rule E3.1 breach by Mikel Arteta |date=14 Dec 2023 |website=The Football Association |access-date=14 Dec 2023 |archive-date=15 Dec 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231215120433/https://www.thefa.com/news/2023/dec/14/update-on-mikel-arteta-charge |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/fa-statement |title=FA statement |date=14 Dec 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=14 Dec 2023 |archive-date=16 Dec 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231216032202/https://www.arsenal.com/news/fa-statement |url-status=live}}</ref> The written reasons published by the regulatory commission stated that Willock, Arsenal academy graduate and the player involved in keeping the ball in play before Gordon gave Newcastle the lead, told Arsenal players "the ball had gone out of play before he crossed into the penalty area".<ref name="The FA v Mikel Arteta FA PDF"/> A footnote in the written reasons said that Arteta "made it clear" during the hearing that he had used the word 'disgrace' with full knowledge of its English connotations.<ref name="The FA v Mikel Arteta FA PDF"/><ref name="Arteta cleared of FA charge TheAthletic"/>

===December===
Arteta's side faced 12th-placed [[Wolverhampton Wanderers F.C.|Wolverhampton Wanderers]] at home on 2 December. Saka's opener in the 6th minute was the Gunners' 100th goal of 2023, making Arsenal the fifth big five European league team to reach this total across all competitions in 2023, after Manchester City, Real Madrid, [[FC Bayern Munich|Bayern Munich]] and Bayer Leverkusen. It also meant that the Gunners had scored at least once in each of their last 32 matches against Wolves in all competitions, the joint longest scoring run against an opponent in the club's history.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.premierleague.com/news/3803402 |title=Arsenal survive late scare to go four points clear at the top |date=2 Dec 2023 |website=Premier League |access-date=3 Dec 2023 |archive-date=3 Dec 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231203030310/https://www.premierleague.com/news/3803402 |url-status=live}}</ref> Ødegaard doubled the lead on 13 minutes. The visitors pulled a goal back in the 86th minute. The 2–1 win kept the Gunners on top of the Premier League table.<ref name="ARS v WOL PL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Dec-02/arsenal-2-1-wolves-match-report |title=Report: Arsenal 2–1 Wolves |last=James |first=Josh |date=2 Dec 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=3 Dec 2023 |archive-date=3 Dec 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231203155731/https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Dec-02/arsenal-2-1-wolves-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref>

Arsenal headed to [[Luton Town F.C.|Luton Town]] on 5 December for their first meeting in the English top flight in 32 years at [[Kenilworth Road]].<ref name="LUT v ARS PL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Dec-05/luton-town-3-4-arsenal-match-report |title=Report: Luton Town 3–4 Arsenal |last=Rogers |first=Jonathon |date=5 Dec 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=6 Dec 2023 |archive-date=7 Dec 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231207180148/https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Dec-05/luton-town-3-4-arsenal-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref> Saka made his 200th senior appearance for the Gunners, becoming the fourth-youngest player to play 200 matches in all competitions for Arsenal.<ref name="LUT v ARS PL">{{cite web |url=https://www.premierleague.com/news/3808753 |title=Rice's last-gasp winner sends Arsenal five points clear |date=5 Dec 2023 |website=Premier League |access-date=6 Dec 2023 |archive-date=6 Dec 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231206075653/https://www.premierleague.com/news/3808753 |url-status=live}}</ref> Martinelli opened the scoring in the 20th minute. The hosts levelled through [[Gabriel Osho]] on 25 minutes. The Gunners regained the lead on 45 minutes as Gabriel Jesus headed home from close range.<ref name="LUT v ARS PL AFC"/> After the start of the second half, strikes from [[Elijah Adebayo]] and [[Ross Barkley]] put the Hatters in front. Arsenal equalised on the hour mark through Havertz's finish. In stoppage time Rice headed in Ødegaard's cross, sparking wild celebrations in the away end. The thrilling 4–3 victory was the first time since 2011 that Arsenal won a Premier League away game in which they had conceded at least three goals. Rice's last-gasp winner at 96 minutes and 23 seconds was the Gunners' latest winning goal on record (since 2006–07) in a Premier League away match, making him the third different Arsenal player to score two 90th minute winning goals in a single Premier League season. The result ended Arsenal's 10-game winless run away against Luton Town in all competitions, earning their first Kenilworth Road win since 1984.<ref name="LUT v ARS PL"/>

The Gunners suffered their second Premier League defeat of the season with a 1–0 loss to 3rd-placed [[Aston Villa F.C.|Aston Villa]] at [[Villa Park]] on 9 December. Manager Arteta watched the game from the stands as he served a one-match touchline ban.<ref name="AVL v ARS PL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Dec-09/aston-villa-1-0-arsenal-match-report |title=Report: Aston Villa 1–0 Arsenal |last=Rogers |first=Jonathon |date=9 Dec 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=10 Dec 2023 |archive-date=10 Dec 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231210103031/https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Dec-09/aston-villa-1-0-arsenal-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref> [[John McGinn]] scored for the hosts on 7 minutes with a shot from the centre of the box, although Arsenal defender White could have done better. The Gunners had a penalty shout in the 47th minute when Villa's [[Douglas Luiz]] caught Gabriel Jesus' ankle inside the box, but VAR quickly decided not to overturn a no-penalty decision.<ref name="AVL v ARS PL BBC">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67598695 |title=Aston Villa 1–0 Arsenal: Villa up to second in Premier League |last=Rindl |first=Joe |date=9 Dec 2023 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=10 Dec 2023 |archive-date=9 Dec 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231209200948/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67598695 |url-status=live}}</ref> An off-the-ball incident occurred in the 87th minute as Nketiah attempted to run in behind Villa defender [[Diego Carlos (footballer, born 1993)|Diego Carlos]], the Arsenal striker was elbowed in the face by the Brazilian, and fell to the ground. Referee [[Jarred Gillett]] showed Carlos a yellow card, but the VAR did not advise Gillett to review the incident on the pitchside monitor for a possible case of violent conduct.<ref>{{cite magazine |url=https://www.si.com/fannation/soccer/futbol/video/diego-carlos-elbows-eddie-nketiah-no-red-card-aston-villa-arsenal |title=Aston Villa's Diego Carlos Lucky To Escape Red Card After Elbow On Arsenal's Eddie Nketiah – Futbol on FanNation |last=Summerscales |first=Robert |date=9 Dec 2023 |magazine=[[Sports Illustrated]] |access-date=10 Dec 2023 |archive-date=12 Dec 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231212073915/https://www.si.com/fannation/soccer/futbol/video/diego-carlos-elbows-eddie-nketiah-no-red-card-aston-villa-arsenal |url-status=live}}</ref> In the 90th minute, Havertz brought down a cross and bundled the ball over the line. The goal was immediately ruled out on the field – a decision that was confirmed by a lengthy VAR check.<ref name="AVL v ARS PL BBC"/> The result meant that Arsenal dropped to second in the league, a point behind leaders Liverpool.<ref name="AVL v ARS PL BBC"/>

With top spot already assured, Arsenal made the trip to the Netherlands on 12 December for the final Champions League group match against Eredivisie side [[PSV Eindhoven]]. In the 42nd minute Nketiah drilled a shot into the bottom corner. The hosts drew level on 50 minutes as [[Yorbe Vertessen]] bent an effort past Ramsdale and in off the post. The game ended 1–1.<ref name="PSV v ARS UCL BBC">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67687847 |title=PSV Eindhoven 1–1 Arsenal: Much-changed Gunners held to Champions League draw |last=Smith |first=Emma |date=12 Dec 2023 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=13 Dec 2023 |archive-date=13 Dec 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231213000604/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/67687847 |url-status=live}}</ref> The Gunners finished the Champions League group stage with the highest goal difference of any team (+12).<ref>{{cite tweet |author=Football on TNT Sports |author-link=TNT Sports (United Kingdom) |user=footballontnt |number=1735291298066702833 |date=14 Dec 2023 |title=Arsenal end the Champions League group stage with the highest goal difference of any team (+12) 🔥 Not bad for their first #UCL campaign in six years... |access-date=14 Dec 2023}}</ref> They would go into the [[2023–24 UEFA Champions League knockout phase#Round of 16|round of 16]] in February 2024.<ref name="PSV v ARS UCL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Dec-12/psv-eindhoven-1-1-arsenal-match-report |title=Report: PSV Eindhoven 1–1 Arsenal |last=James |first=Josh |date=12 Dec 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=13 Dec 2023 |archive-date=13 Dec 2023 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231213031054/https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2023-Dec-12/psv-eindhoven-1-1-arsenal-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref>

