On 4 February, Arteta's side played at home against 1st-placed Liverpool, who had lost only one Premier League game on arrival at Emirates Stadium.<ref name="ARS v LIV PL">{{cite web |url=https://www.premierleague.com/news/3878546 |title=Arsenal shake up title race with BIG win over leaders Liverpool |date=4 Feb 2024 |website=Premier League |access-date=5 Feb 2024 |archive-date=4 Feb 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240204235749/https://www.premierleague.com/news/3878546 |url-status=live}}</ref> This was Arsenal's third meeting with the Reds in the last seven matches, and the 200th league meeting between both sides.<ref name="ARS v LIV PL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2024-Feb-04/arsenal-3-1-liverpool-match-report |title=Report: Arsenal 3–1 Liverpool |last=James |first=Josh |date=4 Feb 2024 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=5 Feb 2024 |archive-date=4 Feb 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240204231636/https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2024-Feb-04/arsenal-3-1-liverpool-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref> Saka opened the scoring in the 14th minute as he tucked home the rebound after goalkeeper Alisson saved Havertz's shot.<ref name="ARS v LIV PL BBC">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/68120819 |title=Arsenal 3–1 Liverpool: Gunners move within two points of Premier League leaders |last=McNulty |first=Phil |date=4 Feb 2024 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=5 Feb 2024 |archive-date=4 Feb 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240204184937/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/68120819 |url-status=live}}</ref> The hosts dominated the first 45 minutes, but Liverpool were level just before half-time without having had a shot on target, as Saliba's indecisiveness allowed Luis Díaz to pass across goal, with the ball inadvertently hitting Gabriel Magalhães before rolling into the net.<ref name="ARS v LIV PL"/> Arsenal retook the lead on 67 minutes when a mix-up between the Reds' Alisson and [[Virgil van Dijk|Van Dijk]] allowed Martinelli to stroke the ball into an empty net.<ref name="ARS v LIV PL BBC"/> Liverpool defender [[Ibrahima Konaté]] was sent off on 88 minutes for a second yellow-card offence after he hauled down the breaking Havertz.<ref name="ARS v LIV PL AFC"/> In second-half stoppage time Kiwior's headed pass found Trossard, who raced away down the left and then scored with a left-footed shot from a narrow angle.<ref name="ARS v LIV PL"/> The 3–1 victory meant that the Gunners were unbeaten in their last four Premier League games against Jürgen Klopp's side, their longest unbeaten run against the Reds in the competition since 2016–17.<ref name="ARS v LIV PL AFC"/> The result put Arsenal two points behind leaders Liverpool.<ref name="ARS v LIV PL BBC"/>

Arsenal faced 7th-placed West Ham United at [[London Stadium]] on 11 February. Saliba broke the deadlock with a header from Rice's corner on 32 minutes. Saka scored his 50th Gunners goal from the penalty spot in the 41st minute. Gabriel Magalhães nodded in a Rice free-kick three minutes later. In first-half stoppage time, Trossard curled home a finish from Ødegaard's pass for the 8,000th league goal in Arsenal's history.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5263209/2024/02/11/west-ham-0-arsenal-6-rice-saka/ |title=West Ham 0 Arsenal 6: Rice's stunning return, Saka's 50th goal and Gabriel's landmark |last=Campbell |first=Jordan |date=11 Feb 2024 |website=The Athletic |access-date=12 Feb 2024 |archive-date=11 Feb 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240211183851/https://theathletic.com/5263209/2024/02/11/west-ham-0-arsenal-6-rice-saka/ |url-status=live}}</ref> In the 63rd minute, Saka collected Ødegaard's pass and rifled into the near post. Two minutes later, Rice fired in a curling shot from 25 yards. The 6–0 victory was the Gunners' biggest Premier League away win and their joint-biggest margin of victory in an away league game since 1935. It was also Arsenal's joint-biggest win in a London derby in league competition.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.premierleague.com/news/3887596 |title=Arsenal score SIX at West Ham to close gap at top |date=11 Feb 2024 |website=Premier League |access-date=12 Feb 2024}}</ref><ref name="WHU v ARS PL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2024-Feb-11/west-ham-united-0-6-arsenal-match-report |title=Report: West Ham United 0–6 Arsenal |last=Rogers |first=Jonathon |date=11 Feb 2024 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=12 Feb 2024 |archive-date=12 Feb 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240212043727/https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2024-Feb-11/west-ham-united-0-6-arsenal-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref>

The Gunners headed to [[Turf Moor]] to take on 19th-placed Burnley on 17 February. Ødegaard gave Arsenal an early lead and Saka struck twice either side of half-time. Trossard then swept home from close range, before Havertz wrapped up the scoring with a solo goal. The 5–0 win meant that the Gunners had begun a calendar year with five successive league victories for the first time in the club's history. It was also the first time Arsenal had scored at least five goals in back-to-back away league games.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.premierleague.com/news/3896376 |title=Arsenal rampant again with five-star victory at Burnley |date=17 Feb 2024 |website=Premier League |access-date=18 Feb 2024}}</ref><ref name="BUR v ARS PL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2024-Feb-17/burnley-0-5-arsenal-match-report |title=Report: Burnley 0–5 Arsenal |last=James |first=Josh |date=17 Feb 2024 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=18 Feb 2024 |archive-date=17 Feb 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240217183829/https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2024-Feb-17/burnley-0-5-arsenal-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref>

On 21 February, Arteta's men travelled to Portugal to face [[FC Porto|Porto]] in the Champions League [[2023–24 UEFA Champions League knockout phase|last-16 first leg]]. The Gunners endured a tricky start and Rice was walking a tightrope for almost the entirety of the contest after he received a yellow card in the second minute. The game lacked cohesion with the stop-start flow suiting the hosts more than it did Arsenal. Neither team was able to break the deadlock until the fourth and final minute of second-half stoppage time, when Martinelli tried to smash a long diagonal to Saka but the ball went straight to Porto defender [[Otávio (footballer, born 2002)|Otávio]], who passed to [[Galeno]], whose long-range curling shot found the back of the net. The result meant that the Portuguese side took a 1–0 lead to north London for the second leg, which would be on 12 March.<ref name="POR v ARS UCL BBC">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/68351916 |title=Porto 1–0 Arsenal: Galeno scores late winner in Champions League last-16 first leg |last=Thomas |first=Marissa |date=21 Feb 2024 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=22 Feb 2024 |archive-date=21 Feb 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240221231707/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/68351916 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="POR v ARS UCL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2024-Feb-21/porto-1-0-arsenal-match-report |title=Report: Porto 1–0 Arsenal |last=James |first=Josh |date=21 Feb 2024 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=22 Feb 2024 |archive-date=22 Feb 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240222022423/https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2024-Feb-21/porto-1-0-arsenal-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/5285891/2024/02/21/porto-arsenal-analysis-result/ |title=Porto 1 Arsenal 0: How damaging is it? Why no shots on target? Did they play like Arsenal? |last1=de Roché |first1=Art |last2=Carey |first2=Mark |date=21 Feb 2024 |website=The Athletic |access-date=22 Feb 2024 |archive-date=22 Feb 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240222134145/https://theathletic.com/5285891/2024/02/21/porto-arsenal-analysis-result/ |url-status=live}}</ref>

Arsenal faced 8th-placed Newcastle United at home on 24 February. The hosts took a 2–0 half-time lead through a [[Sven Botman]] own goal and a Havertz strike. Saka scored in the 65th minute, becoming the first Englishman to score in five consecutive Premier League games for Arsenal since [[Ian Wright]] in 1994. Kiwior added a fourth on 69 minutes. The visitors managed a late consolation courtesy of former Gunner Joe Willock's header. The 4–1 victory saw Arteta's side sit two points behind leaders Liverpool and a point behind Manchester City.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.premierleague.com/news/3908720 |title=Arsenal crush Newcastle to keep pace with title rivals |date=24 Feb 2024 |website=Premier League |access-date=25 Feb 2024}}</ref><ref name="ARS v NEW PL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2024-Feb-24/arsenal-4-1-newcastle-united-match-report |title=Report: Arsenal 4–1 Newcastle United |last=Rogers |first=Jonathon |date=24 Feb 2024 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=25 Feb 2024 |archive-date=25 Feb 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240225010449/https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2024-Feb-24/arsenal-4-1-newcastle-united-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref>

===March===
The Gunners faced 20th-placed Sheffield United away at [[Bramall Lane]] on 4 March. The match saw several records set.<ref name="SHU v ARS PL stats">{{cite web |url=https://www.premierleague.com/news/3922309 |title=The BEST STATS of Arsenal's HUGE WIN at Sheff Utd |date=4 Mar 2024 |website=Premier League |access-date=5 Mar 2024 |archive-date=25 Apr 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240425205121/https://www.premierleague.com/news/3922309 |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="SHU v ARS PL TheAnalyst">{{cite web |url=https://theanalyst.com/na/2024/03/sheffield-united-vs-arsenal-stats/ |title=Sheffield United 0–6 Arsenal Stats |author=Opta Analyst |author-link=Opta Sports |date=5 Mar 2024 |website=The Analyst |access-date=5 Mar 2024 |archive-date=6 Mar 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240306101605/https://theanalyst.com/na/2024/03/sheffield-united-vs-arsenal-stats/ |url-status=live}}</ref> Ødegaard opened the scoring on 5 minutes when he slotted the ball into the bottom corner.<ref name="SHU v ARS PL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2024-Mar-04/sheffield-united-0-6-arsenal-match-report |title=Report: Sheffield United 0–6 Arsenal |last=James |first=Josh |date=4 Mar 2024 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=5 Mar 2024 |archive-date=4 Mar 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240304234000/https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2024-Mar-04/sheffield-united-0-6-arsenal-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref> After Blades defender [[Jayden Bogle]] netted an own goal in the 13th minute,<ref name="SHU v ARS PL BBC">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/68399653 |title=Sheffield United 0–6 Arsenal: Abysmal Blades crushed by ruthless Gunners |last=Smith |first=Emma |date=4 Mar 2024 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=5 Mar 2024 |archive-date=4 Mar 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240304231444/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/68399653 |url-status=live}}</ref> Arsenal became the first team in Premier League history to score at least twice in eight successive halves.<ref name="SHU v ARS PL stats"/> In the 15th minute Kiwior cut the ball back to Martinelli who fired in via a deflection. Ten minutes later, Havertz advanced into the box and rifled a low shot into the corner.<ref name="SHU v ARS PL BBC"/> This goal was the 150,000th scored in English top-flight league history.<ref name="SHU v ARS PL stats"/> Saka registered his 50th assist for Arsenal's first team in all competitions on 39 minutes,<ref name="SHU v ARS PL TheAnalyst"/> as he pulled the ball back for Rice to slide home.<ref name="SHU v ARS PL AFC"/> It meant that the Gunners led 5–0 by the 39th minute, which was the earliest an away side had had a five-goal margin in Premier League history.<ref name="SHU v ARS PL TheAnalyst"/> This was the first time Arsenal had been five goals ahead at half-time in a Premier League match.<ref name="SHU v ARS PL stats"/> In the 58th minute White picked up Havertz's pass in the box and lashed a first-time left-footed effort past home goalkeeper.<ref name="SHU v ARS PL AFC"/> This strike was the 10,000th goal Arsenal had scored in all competitions in their history.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/our-history-told-through-10000-goals |title=Our history, told in our 10,000 goals |last=James |first=Josh |date=6 Mar 2024 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=6 Mar 2024 |archive-date=6 Mar 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240306185312/https://www.arsenal.com/news/our-history-told-through-10000-goals |url-status=live}}</ref><ref name="SHU v ARS PL stats"/> The 6–0 win meant that Arteta's side became the second team in English top-flight history to score five or more goals in three successive away games after Burnley in 1961, and the Gunners were the first side in English league football to win three successive away matches by 5+ goals.<ref name="SHU v ARS PL TheAnalyst"/> The game also saw Arsenal surpass the 300 league goals mark under Arteta's stewardship.<ref name="SHU v ARS PL stats"/>

Arsenal played at home against 15th-placed Brentford on 9 March. Ramsdale made his first Premier League start since the reverse fixture on 25 November as on-loan goalkeeper Raya was ineligible to face his parent club.<ref name="ARS v BRE PL BBC">{{cite web |url=https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/68455049 |title=Arsenal 2–1 Brentford: Kai Havertz winner sends Gunners top of Premier League after Aaron Ramsdale error |last=Jurejko |first=Jonathan |date=9 Mar 2024 |website=BBC Sport |access-date=10 Mar 2024 |archive-date=10 Mar 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240310010322/https://www.bbc.com/sport/football/68455049 |url-status=live}}</ref> The hosts took the lead on 19 minutes when Rice popped up in space to head in White's cross.<ref name="ARS v BRE PL AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2024-Mar-09/arsenal-2-1-brentford-match-report |title=Report: Arsenal 2–1 Brentford |last=Rogers |first=Jonathon |date=9 Mar 2024 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=10 Mar 2024 |archive-date=9 Mar 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240309222206/https://www.arsenal.com/fixture/arsenal/2024-Mar-09/arsenal-2-1-brentford-match-report |url-status=live}}</ref> From that point on the Gunners looked in control until the fourth minute of first-half stoppage time when Ramsdale made a major error. The English goalkeeper dawdled on a routine backpass in his six-yard box under little pressure and took too long on a clearance, which allowed Brentford forward [[Yoane Wissa]] to close down and block it into the net.<ref name="ARS v BRE PL BBC"/><ref name="ARS v BRE PL">{{cite web |url=https://www.premierleague.com/news/3925574 |title=Havertz spares Ramsdale's blushes to send Arsenal top |date=9 Mar 2024 |website=Premier League |access-date=10 Mar 2024 |archive-date=10 Mar 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240310045643/https://www.premierleague.com/news/3925574 |url-status=live}}</ref> Arteta's side pushed for a second-half winner without much luck until the 86th minute when Havertz nodded in White's cross from close range.<ref name="ARS v BRE PL AFC"/> The goal made him the first German to score in four consecutive games in Premier League history.<ref>{{cite tweet |author=OptaFranz |author-link=Opta Sports |user=OptaFranz |number=1767197250546008339 |date=11 Mar 2024 |title=4 – @Arsenal's Kai Havertz has scored in each of his last four Premier League appearances (4 goals), making him the first German to score in four consecutive matches in the competition's history. Wunderbar. |access-date=11 Mar 2024}}</ref> The 2–1 victory meant that the Gunners had won eight consecutive Premier League matches for the first time since April 2015 under Arsène Wenger,<ref name="ARS v BRE PL AFC"/> and they became the fourth side to win each of their first eight Premier League games of a calendar year.<ref name="ARS v BRE PL"/> The result sent them back to the top of the league table, before Liverpool and Manchester City drew against each other on the following day.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.premierleague.com/news/3926849 |title=Liverpool and Man City draw to leave Arsenal TOP of table |date=10 Mar 2024 |website=Premier League |access-date=11 Mar 2024 |archive-date=12 Mar 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20240312020330/https://www.premierleague.com/news/3926849 |url-status=live}}</ref>

