===Kit information===
This is Adidas's fifth year supplying Arsenal kit, having taken over from [[Puma (brand)|Puma]] at the beginning of the 2019–20 season.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/adidas-partnership-extended-2030 |title=adidas partnership extended to 2030 |date=30 Sep 2022 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=1 Jun 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://news.adidas.com/football/adidas-and-arsenal-launch-new-partnership-with-2019-20-home-kit/s/a792ee1b-7f39-4f66-a095-a689e151ec5b |title=adidas and Arsenal launch new partnership with 2019/20 home kit |date=1 Jul 2019 |website=Adidas |access-date=1 Jun 2023}}</ref> On 2 August 2023, Arsenal and Emirates announced that they had extended their partnership to 2028 – the longest-running front-of-shirt sponsorship in Premier League history.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/arsenal-and-emirates-extend-partnership-2028 |title=Arsenal and Emirates extend partnership to 2028 |date=2 Aug 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=2 Aug 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.nytimes.com/athletic/4742050/2023/08/02/arsenal-shirt-sponsor-emirates-deal/ |title=Arsenal extend shirt sponsorship deal with Emirates until 2028 |last=Burrows |first=Ben |date=2 Aug 2023 |website=The Athletic |access-date=2 Aug 2023}}</ref>

[[File:RC Lens - Arsenal FC (03-10-2023) 34.jpg|thumb|right|250px|Arsenal players wearing the third kit in their Champions League away game against Lens on 3 October 2023]]
*'''Home:''' The club confirmed on 26 May 2023 that their new home kit for the 2023–24 season would debut in the final home game of the 2022–23 season. The home kit uses Arsenal's traditional colours of red and white. The shirt has a red body and white sleeves, and is complemented by white shorts and white socks. Red socks were used in some away games when there was a colour clash with the home team's kit. The new kit pays tribute to the 20th anniversary of the [[2003–04 Arsenal F.C. season|2003–04]] [[The Invincibles (English football)|Invincibles]] season, as the Gunners' crest, Adidas's logo and [[three stripes]] feature in gold, while a lightning bolt pattern appears on the socks.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/introducing-our-new-202324-adidas-home-kit |title=Introducing our new 2023/24 adidas home kit |date=26 May 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=1 Jun 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/gallery-closer-look-our-202324-home-kit |title=Gallery: A closer look at our 2023/24 home kit |date=26 May 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=1 Jun 2023}}</ref>
*'''Away:''' The new men's team away kit was revealed on 18 July, during the club's US tour. The shirt features black lines inspired by the map of [[London Borough of Islington|Islington]], Arsenal's home borough. A yellow base colour is complemented by light blue accents on the collars and sleeves. The shirt is partnered with black shorts and yellow socks.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/arsenal-release-new-202324-mens-away-kit-0 |title=Arsenal release new 2023/24 men's away kit |date=18 Jul 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=18 Jul 2023}}</ref><ref name="2023 US Tour AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/stay-date-our-2023-us-tour |title=2023 US Tour Hub |date=19 Jul 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=19 Jul 2023}}</ref> The kit was launched with an accompanying video that shows a fictional radio station set deep within Emirates Stadium broadcasting "Islington's finest to the world".<ref name="2023 US Tour AFC"/><ref>{{cite AV media |date=18 Jul 2023 |title=Introducing the new Arsenal x adidas 23/24 Men's Team away kit |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=gmIPqbKE54w |access-date=18 Jul 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |via=YouTube}}</ref> The kit debuted in the [[2023 MLS All-Star Game|2023 Major League Soccer All-Star Game]] on July 19.<ref name="MLS v ARS Friendly AFC"/>
*'''Third:''' On 18 August, the Gunners unveiled their new third kit, which pays homage to their green and navy-blue away kit from the [[1982–83 Arsenal F.C. season|1982–83 season]]. The shirt has a green base with navy shoulders and a simple off-white cannon badge at chest, and is combined with navy shorts and green socks.<ref name="Third kit AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/arsenal-and-adidas-launch-202324-third-kit |title=Arsenal and adidas launch 2023/24 third kit |date=18 Aug 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=18 Aug 2023}}</ref><ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/take-closer-look-our-202324-third-kit |title=Take a closer look at our 2023/24 third kit |date=18 Aug 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=18 Aug 2023}}</ref> White socks were used in some away games when there was a colour clash with the home team's kit. The kit was launched alongside a film that "brings continental style to the streets of Islington".<ref name="Third kit AFC"/><ref>{{cite AV media |date=18 Aug 2023 |title=Introducing the new Arsenal x adidas 23/24 third kit |url=https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=dBdF-ySqB8g |access-date=18 Aug 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |via=YouTube}}</ref> The kit debuted in Arsenal's UEFA Champions League group stage match against French side [[RC Lens|Lens]] on 3 October.<ref name="LEN v ARS UCL AFC"/>
*'''No More Red:''' On 4 January 2024, Arsenal announced that they would extend their "No More Red" campaign – an initiative that aims to help keep young people safe from knife crime and youth violence – for a third season. The all-white kit was worn for the first time in a home fixture on 7 January when they would face Liverpool in the FA Cup third round.<ref name="No More Red kit AFC">{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/arsenal-and-adidas-relaunch-no-more-red-2024 |title=Arsenal and adidas relaunch No More Red for 2024 |date=4 Jan 2024 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=4 Jan 2024}}</ref>
*'''Goalkeeper:''' The new goalkeeper kits are based on Adidas's goalkeeper template for the season.

