==Pre-season and friendlies==
<!-- Update source: https://www.arsenal.com/results -->
On 21 March 2023, Arsenal announced that they would travel to the United States in July to compete against the [[MLS All-Star Game|MLS All-Stars]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/were-facing-mls-all-stars-summer |title=We're facing the MLS All-Stars this summer! |date=21 Mar 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=1 Jun 2023}}</ref> On 28 April, a further US tour friendly was confirmed against [[Manchester United F.C.|Manchester United]] in New Jersey in July.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/arsenal-play-manchester-united-new-york |title=Arsenal to play Manchester United in New Jersey |date=28 Apr 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=1 Jun 2023}}</ref> On 12 May, Arsenal announced their third and final pre-season fixture in the US this summer, against [[FC Barcelona|Barcelona]] at [[SoFi Stadium]], the home to the [[National Football League]]'s [[Los Angeles Rams]] which is also owned by [[Kroenke Sports and Entertainment]].<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/arsenal-play-barcelona-los-angeles |title=Arsenal to play Barcelona in Los Angeles |date=12 May 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=1 Jun 2023}}</ref> The Gunners confirmed on 8 June that they would travel to Germany to face [[1. FC Nürnberg]] as part of a pre-season training camp at the [[Adidas]] headquarters in July, before heading to the US.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/pre-season-friendly-against-fc-nurnberg-confirmed |title=Pre-season friendly against FC Nurnberg confirmed |date=8 Jun 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=8 Jun 2023}}</ref> A day later, the club announced the return of the [[Emirates Cup]] with [[AS Monaco FC|Monaco]] confirmed as opponents.<ref>{{cite web |url=https://www.arsenal.com/news/monaco-confirmed-2023-emirates-cup-opponents |title=AS Monaco confirmed as 2023 Emirates Cup opponents |date=9 Jun 2023 |website=Arsenal FC |access-date=9 Jun 2023}}</ref>

